{"sourceSha256": "3c6b386b13da61c7c60ebf2aeda3e03ced361acdac5556601b0aa82bef160ae7", "text": "Question 5\nNot yet answered\n\nMarked out of 1.00\n\nP Flag question\n\nInformation\n\nP Flag question\n\nThe purpose of the safety notice about sharps injuries is to\n\nselect one:\nA. praise staff who have been following sharps protocols.\nB. reduce the frequency of future sharps harm to staff.\n\nC. remind staff about the risks of working with sharps.\n\nHospital Bulletin Board Safety Alert Communication\n\nSituation\n® Last week, there were 4 reported sharps injuries at the Medical\nCentre in a 6 day period.\n© In comparison, there were 18 sharps injuries in the previous\ncalendar year, about 1-2 per month.\nBackground\n\ne Although we have gone many weeks without an employee lost time\ninjury, sharps injuries can be potentially serious events.\n\nAssessment\n\ne A thorough cause analysis investigation completed with staff\ninvolved, their managers and the occupational health and safety\nteam, revealed that each of these injuries was preventable.\n\nRecommendation\n\ne Verify and Validate: Verify that safety features available on\nsharps have fully engaged before transporting or discarding a\nneedle. Complete a visual check and listen for the ‘click’.\n\n¢ STAR: Make sure your fingers are not in the path of a needle\nwhen holding soft tissue for injection.\n\ne Seek Help: If required, obtain assistance from a co-worker\nbefore injecting a patient.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Question 5\nNot yet answered\n\nMarked out of 1.00\n\nP Flag question\n\nInformation\n\nP Flag question\n\nThe purpose of the safety notice about sharps injuries is to\n\nselect one:\nA. praise staff who have been following sharps protocols.\nB. reduce the frequency of future sharps harm to staff.\n\nC. remind staff about the risks of working with sharps.\n\nHospital Bulletin Board Safety Alert Communication\n\nSituation\n® Last week, there were 4 reported sharps injuries at the Medical\nCentre in a 6 day period.\n© In comparison, there were 18 sharps injuries in the previous\ncalendar year, about 1-2 per month.\nBackground\n\ne Although we have gone many weeks without an employee lost time\ninjury, sharps injuries can be potentially serious events.\n\nAssessment\n\ne A thorough cause analysis investigation completed with staff\ninvolved, their managers and the occupational health and safety\nteam, revealed that each of these injuries was preventable.\n\nRecommendation\n\ne Verify and Validate: Verify that safety features available on\nsharps have fully engaged before transporting or discarding a\nneedle. Complete a visual check and listen for the ‘click’.\n\n¢ STAR: Make sure your fingers are not in the path of a needle\nwhen holding soft tissue for injection.\n\ne Seek Help: If required, obtain assistance from a co-worker\nbefore injecting a patient.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2800.0, "height": 2651.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Question 5\nNot yet answered", "lines": [{"text": "Question 5", "x": 0.0175, "y": 0.00679, "width": 0.0675, "height": 0.02075, "confidence": 0.968, "words": [{"text": "Question", "x": 0.0175, "width": 0.06714, "confidence": 0.966}, {"text": "5", "x": 0.07643, "width": 0.00857, "confidence": 0.969}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Not yet answered", "x": 0.01786, "y": 0.04149, "width": 0.09857, "height": 0.01207, "confidence": 0.962, "words": [{"text": "Not", "x": 0.01786, "width": 0.01964, "confidence": 0.961}, {"text": "yet", "x": 0.04071, "width": 0.01857, "confidence": 0.964}, {"text": "answered", "x": 0.06321, "width": 0.05321, "confidence": 0.961}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Marked out of 1.00", "lines": [{"text": "Marked out of 1.00", "x": 0.01714, "y": 0.07507, "width": 0.1075, "height": 0.00981, "confidence": 0.962, "words": [{"text": "Marked", "x": 0.01714, "width": 0.04071, "confidence": 0.955}, {"text": "out", "x": 0.06214, "width": 0.01929, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "of", "x